cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata in this file."
title: "AuthGuard: bot defence for the ILIAS account-registration form"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "OC Open Consulting SB Srl"
    website: "https://www.oc-group.eu"
    email: "plugins@oc-group.eu"
abstract: >-
  ILIAS plugin that rejects automated submissions of the self-registration form.
  It generates a CAPTCHA image on the ILIAS server itself, contacts no
  third-party service, and adds invisible checks that ask a legitimate visitor
  for nothing: each code is single-use, image regeneration is throttled per
  session, and a submission arriving less than two seconds after the form was
  displayed is refused. ILIAS core shipped a CAPTCHA on that form up to ILIAS 7
  and removed it in ILIAS 8 on the grounds that it no longer kept bots out; this
  plugin restores the protection as a user-interface hook plugin, without any
  change to the ILIAS core.
version: 9.1.0
date-released: "2026-08-20"
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/oc-group/ilias-uihk_authguard"
